WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.815 --> 00:00:10.089
Welcome to Preshift Rota, a joint venture between Williams, Stanley and Co.

2
00:00:10.089 --> 00:00:11.004
and Preshift.

3
00:00:11.004 --> 00:00:14.590
Every rota tool on the market answers one question:

4
00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:15.997
who is working when.

5
00:00:15.997 --> 00:00:20.427
Preshift answers the question an operator actually cares about.

6
00:00:20.427 --> 00:00:25.983
What will this week's labour cost me against what I will take, and is it legal?

7
00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:31.870
It builds the rota from the sales forecast, costs every shift the way payroll will, blocks

8
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:37.426
anything that breaks UK employment law, and hands finance a ready to post labour accrual, so

9
00:00:37.426 --> 00:00:41.050
the P and L carries true labour before payroll has even run.

10
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.323
This is the public demo.

11
00:00:43.323 --> 00:00:47.121
Anyone can start a private copy of a sample group:

12
00:00:47.121 --> 00:00:52.211
two companies, three London sites, real teams, rates and forecasts.

13
00:00:52.211 --> 00:00:56.921
Nobody else sees what you change, and it is wiped at midnight.

14
00:00:56.921 --> 00:00:58.516
Press Start the demo.

15
00:00:58.975 --> 00:01:03.994
Each Monday, What's new offers that week's changes as a short walkthrough.

16
00:01:03.994 --> 00:01:07.793
One card per change, each opening the screen it changed.

17
00:01:07.793 --> 00:01:13.084
It only shows the changes for sections you use, and it is offered once a week.

18
00:01:13.084 --> 00:01:14.983
Let's look at the first few.

19
00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:20.745
Next takes you to the following change, on its own screen, with the right site and

20
00:01:20.745 --> 00:01:21.911
view already open.

21
00:01:21.911 --> 00:01:26.834
Two minutes, and nobody has to read a release note to find out what changed.

22
00:01:27.285 --> 00:01:32.226
You can replay it any time from What's new at the foot of the left-hand bar.

23
00:01:32.226 --> 00:01:34.437
Let's close it and start the tour.

24
00:01:38.616 --> 00:01:44.175
The left-hand bar groups the work the way a general manager runs the week.

25
00:01:44.175 --> 00:01:44.776
Plan it.

26
00:01:44.776 --> 00:01:46.429
Run the hours and pay.

27
00:01:46.429 --> 00:01:47.931
Look after the team.

28
00:01:47.931 --> 00:01:51.462
Then the money, and the organisation behind it.

29
00:01:51.462 --> 00:01:55.368
Groups fold away, and the one you are in stays open.

30
00:01:55.819 --> 00:02:01.380
Everyone sees only the sections their roles allow, and an owner can switch off whole features

31
00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:06.044
the business does not use, so a GM is not wading through forty sections to use

32
00:02:06.044 --> 00:02:06.283
ten.

33
00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:09.739
Go to a section finds any screen by name.

34
00:02:09.739 --> 00:02:14.942
Press the slash key from anywhere, type a few letters, and press enter.

35
00:02:15.393 --> 00:02:20.497
In the demo, Viewing as lets you see the product as any of thirteen people:

36
00:02:20.497 --> 00:02:24.717
a general manager, a supervisor, a chef, the finance director.

37
00:02:24.717 --> 00:02:30.297
Each sees exactly what their roles permit, and the server enforces the same rules.

38
00:02:30.748 --> 00:02:35.364
At the top of every week screen sits the week picker, with arrows either side, and

39
00:02:35.364 --> 00:02:39.868
a badge telling you whether this week is published to the team or still a draft.

40
00:02:44.676 --> 00:02:52.571
Along the bottom, Tell Preshift takes plain English instructions, and Shifty, in the corner, answers questions.

41
00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:54.420
We will come back to both.

42
00:02:58.587 --> 00:03:02.323
Sites puts every site side by side, grouped by company.

43
00:03:02.323 --> 00:03:09.047
Forecast sales, loaded labour cost, labour as a percentage of sales against each site's own target,

44
00:03:09.047 --> 00:03:15.363
the variance in pounds, sales per labour hour, paid hours, and whether the rota is published.

45
00:03:15.814 --> 00:03:21.303
Each company carries a subtotal, and the group line uses a sales weighted target, so a

46
00:03:21.303 --> 00:03:24.622
large site cannot hide a small one that has drifted.

47
00:03:25.072 --> 00:03:27.243
On the right, the rota P and L.

48
00:03:27.243 --> 00:03:33.968
Forecast sales, then wages, holiday accrual, employer N I and pension, the labour cost that will

49
00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:37.470
tie to the journal, and contribution after labour.

50
00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:41.392
Underneath, labour percentage day by day against target.

51
00:03:41.392 --> 00:03:43.984
It sits beside every planning screen.

52
00:03:44.435 --> 00:03:45.301
Further down:

53
00:03:45.301 --> 00:03:51.427
rest overrides published in the last four weeks, cross site cover, and travel between sites.

54
00:03:51.427 --> 00:03:56.489
Journey times come from the T f L planner, so the rota blocks a move between

55
00:03:56.489 --> 00:03:59.219
two sites that nobody could make in time.

56
00:03:59.669 --> 00:04:03.576
And one press of Build from forecast builds every site in scope:

57
00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:08.521
each site with its own team first, then cover from people who have agreed to work

58
00:04:08.521 --> 00:04:09.437
at other sites.

59
00:04:13.605 --> 00:04:16.853
Open a site, and you land on its rota.

60
00:04:16.853 --> 00:04:18.477
This is Marylebone.

61
00:04:18.928 --> 00:04:24.059
Coming up flags what this week needs your view on, read from the calendar, the weather

62
00:04:24.059 --> 00:04:25.073
and the bookings:

63
00:04:25.073 --> 00:04:30.979
half term starts today, Halloween on Saturday, a party of twenty four, and Saturday dinner bookings

64
00:04:30.979 --> 00:04:33.544
running at more than double the usual pace.

65
00:04:33.995 --> 00:04:36.907
The service timeline is the default view.

66
00:04:36.907 --> 00:04:43.015
Each day is drawn over its own forecast sales curve, with shifts as bars grouped front

67
00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:45.359
of house, bar, and back of house.

68
00:04:45.359 --> 00:04:49.691
Every bar shows the person, the role, the hours and its cost.

69
00:04:50.142 --> 00:04:55.272
Beside each day, that day's labour and its labour percentage against target.

70
00:04:55.272 --> 00:05:01.278
Monday is quiet and carries guaranteed hours, so it shows red, and you know exactly where

71
00:05:01.278 --> 00:05:01.818
to look.

72
00:05:01.818 --> 00:05:06.678
The strip beneath each day reads the hours short or over against demand.

73
00:05:07.129 --> 00:05:12.297
Scroll down, and the rest of the week follows, day by day, each with its own

74
00:05:12.297 --> 00:05:14.065
curve and its own P and L.

75
00:05:18.236 --> 00:05:20.131
Click any shift to open it.

76
00:05:20.131 --> 00:05:24.342
The number that matters is what this shift adds to the week.

77
00:05:24.342 --> 00:05:26.377
Not a naive rate times hours.

78
00:05:26.377 --> 00:05:31.290
Marco is on forty guaranteed hours, so this shift adds nothing at all:

79
00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:33.956
the business pays that gap either way.

80
00:05:34.407 --> 00:05:36.368
The law is checked as you type.

81
00:05:36.368 --> 00:05:41.995
Cut the unpaid break below the legal minimum and Preshift tells you what the Working Time

82
00:05:41.995 --> 00:05:44.967
Regulations require for a shift of this length.

83
00:05:45.418 --> 00:05:50.877
Ask for cover puts this shift out to everyone who could legally take it.

84
00:05:50.877 --> 00:05:52.090
For now, cancel.

85
00:05:52.541 --> 00:05:56.844
Now Chloe, a bartender paid by the hour with no guaranteed hours.

86
00:05:56.844 --> 00:05:59.227
Her shift adds its full loaded cost:

87
00:05:59.227 --> 00:06:05.316
gross pay, holiday accrual at twelve point oh seven percent, employer N I at fifteen percent

88
00:06:05.316 --> 00:06:08.494
above the threshold, and auto enrolment pension.

89
00:06:08.494 --> 00:06:13.789
On costs are worked on the whole week and then spread across shifts, so the rota

90
00:06:13.789 --> 00:06:15.245
reconciles to payroll.

91
00:06:15.695 --> 00:06:18.632
You can also work straight on the timeline.

92
00:06:18.632 --> 00:06:23.549
Drag a bar to move it, or drag either end to change the hours in fifteen

93
00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:24.437
minute steps.

94
00:06:24.437 --> 00:06:28.398
Cost, labour percentage and compliance update as you drag.

95
00:06:28.398 --> 00:06:33.862
A shift that has already started is locked, so when we try to cut Ellie's shift,

96
00:06:33.862 --> 00:06:37.823
which is under way tonight, Preshift refuses and says why.

97
00:06:38.273 --> 00:06:42.454
Drag across empty space on a day to draw a new shift, or click a red,

98
00:06:42.454 --> 00:06:46.029
short hour to fill that gap with the role that is shortest.

99
00:06:46.029 --> 00:06:51.967
The picker ranks who should work it, trained and available, cheapest first, and offers people from

100
00:06:51.967 --> 00:06:56.753
the group's other sites who are set up to cover, with the reason anyone cannot.

101
00:07:00.913 --> 00:07:03.133
Next week has not been started.

102
00:07:03.133 --> 00:07:09.721
Rather than copying last week's rota and hoping, Preshift builds it from the sales forecast.

103
00:07:10.171 --> 00:07:16.263
It turns hourly forecast sales and covers into headcount for each role, then fills the gaps

104
00:07:16.263 --> 00:07:21.350
peak first, with the cheapest legal person, and trims the overstaffed edges.

105
00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:22.555
Watch the P and L.

106
00:07:23.004 --> 00:07:26.074
Built, costed and inside the labour budget.

107
00:07:26.074 --> 00:07:32.071
Gaps that cannot be filled legally with the current team are never hidden or forced.

108
00:07:32.071 --> 00:07:37.425
They are reported as a hiring or cross training signal, not a rota problem.

109
00:07:37.425 --> 00:07:39.780
Here, the site is short of hosts.

110
00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:45.320
Scroll down and the whole week is there, every shift on its curve, ready to check

111
00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:47.142
and adjust before publishing.

112
00:07:47.592 --> 00:07:51.474
At the foot of the P and L sit compliance and sign off.

113
00:07:51.474 --> 00:07:56.767
Blocking issues stop publication, so nothing illegal ever reaches the team.

114
00:07:56.767 --> 00:08:01.848
Once it is clean, publish, and each person hears about their own shifts.

115
00:08:06.015 --> 00:08:10.041
By person shows every person across the week as a grid.

116
00:08:10.041 --> 00:08:13.407
Drag a shift to another person or another day.

117
00:08:13.859 --> 00:08:19.429
The Gantt view gives one line per person, with shifts as bars against the clock:

118
00:08:19.429 --> 00:08:22.144
the whole week, or one day by the hour.

119
00:08:22.144 --> 00:08:27.087
Drag to move or hand over a shift, and drag across an empty line to add

120
00:08:27.087 --> 00:08:27.365
one.

121
00:08:27.365 --> 00:08:31.403
At a site split into areas, it groups and filters by area.

122
00:08:31.854 --> 00:08:36.894
Cover map lays the whole week against demand in one grid, so you see where to

123
00:08:36.894 --> 00:08:38.531
add or cut the next hour.

124
00:08:38.531 --> 00:08:40.494
Click a short hour to fill it.

125
00:08:40.944 --> 00:08:45.796
Rest shows last week and this week as one line per person, so a close before

126
00:08:45.796 --> 00:08:50.136
an open, or a long run of days, shows up before it becomes a breach.

127
00:08:50.586 --> 00:08:53.061
Positions takes one day by position:

128
00:08:53.061 --> 00:08:57.941
who is on the bar, the pass, the door, hour by hour, and where a needed

129
00:08:57.941 --> 00:08:59.178
position is empty.

130
00:08:59.629 --> 00:09:04.578
Shift cost stacks each shift at its loaded cost against the day target.

131
00:09:04.578 --> 00:09:09.109
When labour runs over, this is how you choose which shift to cut.

132
00:09:09.559 --> 00:09:15.199
Changes shows who the next publish will tell, and what, before anyone is told.

133
00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:22.276
And Fairness looks back over four weeks of weekends, closes, late finishes and hours under contract,

134
00:09:22.276 --> 00:09:25.058
to show who keeps getting the hard shifts.

135
00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:27.121
Nine views, one week.

136
00:09:27.121 --> 00:09:32.566
The How to guide sets out the order to use them before a rota goes out.

137
00:09:36.736 --> 00:09:40.800
Ask the assistant lets a GM say what they need in plain English.

138
00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:44.863
Ben is off Saturday, re cover the bar without going over target.

139
00:09:44.863 --> 00:09:50.768
Claude drafts the week by calling the engine's own costing and compliance tools, so it cannot

140
00:09:50.768 --> 00:09:55.720
roster anything illegal, and it leaves shifts that have already started alone.

141
00:09:56.171 --> 00:10:01.910
It works for one site, a company, or the whole group, and nothing changes until you

142
00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.776
review and apply the draft.

143
00:10:03.776 --> 00:10:06.473
In this public demo it is switched off.

144
00:10:06.473 --> 00:10:11.243
On your own account it runs live, and an owner can turn it on or off.

145
00:10:11.693 --> 00:10:18.826
Shifty, in the bottom right, answers questions about the rota, labour, the team and holiday from

146
00:10:18.826 --> 00:10:20.238
the app's own data.

147
00:10:20.238 --> 00:10:21.576
Who is on tonight.

148
00:10:21.576 --> 00:10:24.251
What is labour running at this week.

149
00:10:24.251 --> 00:10:26.405
Who has holiday left to take.

150
00:10:26.855 --> 00:10:32.927
And Tell Preshift, along the bottom, or Control K, takes one line instructions.

151
00:10:32.927 --> 00:10:34.310
Add a new starter.

152
00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:36.692
Ben is ill tonight, find cover.

153
00:10:36.692 --> 00:10:41.303
Each change is shown to you and confirmed before it happens.

154
00:10:45.463 --> 00:10:49.330
Staff ask in the staff app, and the manager decides here.

155
00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:53.739
Holiday, time off, sickness, availability, swaps and open shifts.

156
00:10:53.739 --> 00:10:59.302
Every request is checked again when you approve it, by the same rules as the rota,

157
00:10:59.302 --> 00:11:05.407
so a swap that would break the Working Time Regulations or double book someone is stopped.

158
00:11:05.858 --> 00:11:10.789
Shifts going is one way to put a shift out, whether someone cannot work it or

159
00:11:10.789 --> 00:11:11.814
nobody is on it.

160
00:11:11.814 --> 00:11:18.025
Preshift shows everyone who could legally take it, cheapest first, with what each adds to labour,

161
00:11:18.025 --> 00:11:20.330
and why anyone else is not eligible.

162
00:11:20.781 --> 00:11:22.302
You choose who hears:

163
00:11:22.302 --> 00:11:28.168
everyone eligible now, the cheapest first in rounds, or only the people you tick.

164
00:11:28.168 --> 00:11:29.327
And who decides:

165
00:11:29.327 --> 00:11:33.744
the manager approves a claim, or the first legal yes gets it.

166
00:11:33.744 --> 00:11:37.365
Staff answer in the app, or reply YES on WhatsApp.

167
00:11:37.816 --> 00:11:40.714
Approve claims automatically, site by site.

168
00:11:40.714 --> 00:11:45.903
A claim is approved the moment it is made only when it breaks no rule, raises

169
00:11:45.903 --> 00:11:51.025
nothing to review, and keeps the site's labour that week at or under target.

170
00:11:51.025 --> 00:11:52.912
Anything else waits for you.

171
00:11:57.074 --> 00:12:00.227
The forecast is built from the site's own till.

172
00:12:00.227 --> 00:12:06.063
The same weekday and hour over the last eight weeks, recent weeks counting most, with a

173
00:12:06.063 --> 00:12:07.405
damped trend on top.

174
00:12:07.405 --> 00:12:13.106
Bank holidays trade like past bank holidays, or like a Sunday until there is history.

175
00:12:13.556 --> 00:12:16.459
Then tell the model what it cannot know.

176
00:12:16.459 --> 00:12:19.579
A heatwave, a match down the road, a refit.

177
00:12:19.579 --> 00:12:25.820
Each adjustment is applied as a multiplier, with its reason, when the model next runs.

178
00:12:26.271 --> 00:12:32.708
Demand turns that forecast into headcount for each role, hour by hour, using sales per labour

179
00:12:32.708 --> 00:12:36.031
hour or covers per person, with floors and caps.

180
00:12:36.031 --> 00:12:38.799
Pick a day to see rostered against plan.

181
00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:45.394
Rework from past takings recalibrates those standards from what the site actually traded.

182
00:12:45.845 --> 00:12:48.963
The calendar has the UK trading year built in:

183
00:12:48.963 --> 00:12:54.521
Easter, Mothering Sunday, Halloween, Black Friday, Mad Friday, every bank holiday.

184
00:12:54.521 --> 00:13:01.367
Weather and local events are fetched every morning, bookings come in from the reservation system, and

185
00:13:01.367 --> 00:13:03.197
school holidays by council.

186
00:13:03.648 --> 00:13:06.235
Each item says what to do about it.

187
00:13:06.235 --> 00:13:07.935
A party of twenty four:

188
00:13:07.935 --> 00:13:09.561
roster for it by name.

189
00:13:09.561 --> 00:13:13.256
Saturday dinner pacing at more than double normal:

190
00:13:13.256 --> 00:13:17.247
build the forecast again and check the rota covers it.

191
00:13:17.247 --> 00:13:19.464
Mark it done, or set it aside.

192
00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:28.783
Coach offers the three changes to this week that save the most without leaving the floor

193
00:13:28.783 --> 00:13:30.245
short or breaking a rule.

194
00:13:30.245 --> 00:13:35.096
Trim an overstaffed edge, take off a shift that is over demand all the way through,

195
00:13:35.096 --> 00:13:38.544
or give a shift to someone cheaper who is trained and free.

196
00:13:38.995 --> 00:13:45.411
Each move shows the saving, loaded with holiday, N I and pension, and the labour percentage

197
00:13:45.411 --> 00:13:46.046
after it.

198
00:13:46.046 --> 00:13:49.219
Take it, and the rota changes there and then.

199
00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:51.055
Below, the ladder.

200
00:13:51.055 --> 00:13:52.593
Four rungs of habit:

201
00:13:52.593 --> 00:13:59.440
the rota on time and legal, labour on target, daypart precision, and owning the forecast.

202
00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:03.441
A site on target with a late rota is lucky, not run.

203
00:14:03.441 --> 00:14:06.518
Coach the habits and the results follow.

204
00:14:10.684 --> 00:14:15.658
Clock in turns a tablet at the staff entrance into a sign in point.

205
00:14:15.658 --> 00:14:21.002
Staff tap an RFID card, or a phone's NFC, or sign in by name, inside the

206
00:14:21.002 --> 00:14:22.190
site's geofence.

207
00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:26.644
It lists who is on today's rota and whether they are in yet.

208
00:14:27.095 --> 00:14:32.627
Signing in by name only works on a device inside the geofence, so nobody clocks in

209
00:14:32.627 --> 00:14:33.505
from the bus.

210
00:14:33.505 --> 00:14:38.767
A shared iPad can also be paired as a kiosk that does nothing but clock people

211
00:14:38.767 --> 00:14:40.319
in and out at one site.

212
00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:43.388
Cut call is for the middle of service.

213
00:14:43.388 --> 00:14:48.210
Trading so far from the till is set against forecast to give the pace.

214
00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:53.722
The rest of the day is reforecast at that pace and turned back into headcount by

215
00:14:53.722 --> 00:14:54.066
role.

216
00:14:54.516 --> 00:14:59.505
When trade is behind, it names who to send home early, and the saving is worked

217
00:14:59.505 --> 00:15:05.189
on each person's whole week, after guaranteed hours and the N I and pension thresholds, so

218
00:15:05.189 --> 00:15:07.778
it is what payroll will actually not pay.

219
00:15:07.778 --> 00:15:09.673
Apply, and the shifts are cut.

220
00:15:09.673 --> 00:15:15.420
Tonight Marylebone is already as lean as the reforecast allows, so there is nothing to cut.

221
00:15:19.582 --> 00:15:23.686
Payroll runs as five steps, straight through to TeamPay.

222
00:15:23.686 --> 00:15:28.597
In the demo, TeamPay is a simulator, so we can run the whole thing.

223
00:15:28.597 --> 00:15:33.214
First, the people go into TeamPay, one PAYE scheme per company.

224
00:15:33.665 --> 00:15:35.481
Second, clocked hours.

225
00:15:35.481 --> 00:15:39.113
We simulate a week of clocking for the site.

226
00:15:39.564 --> 00:15:45.443
Finished shifts with less rest break than the law gives are flagged before approval, as too

227
00:15:45.443 --> 00:15:46.412
short or split.

228
00:15:46.412 --> 00:15:52.033
What do I do explains the fix, and the manager approves each person's hours against the

229
00:15:52.033 --> 00:15:52.356
rota.

230
00:15:52.807 --> 00:15:53.925
Third, approve.

231
00:15:53.925 --> 00:16:01.152
Fourth, send the approved hours to TeamPay, one batch per company, through an outbox that retries

232
00:16:01.152 --> 00:16:02.791
and never sends twice.

233
00:16:04.015 --> 00:16:09.013
Fifth, the pay run comes back on a signed webhook and is reconciled to the accrual,

234
00:16:09.013 --> 00:16:13.831
so finance sees the difference between what the rota said and what payroll paid.

235
00:16:17.999 --> 00:16:24.398
Clocked versus rota sets clocked hours against the rota by cause, before they are approved:

236
00:16:24.398 --> 00:16:27.070
late starts, early finishes, overruns.

237
00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:32.063
It fills in as each day closes, with the week's labour flash alongside.

238
00:16:32.514 --> 00:16:38.426
Tronc splits every penny of tips and service charge on clocked hours, so whoever stayed for

239
00:16:38.426 --> 00:16:40.050
the close is paid for it.

240
00:16:40.050 --> 00:16:46.806
Run by an independent troncmaster, the payments carry income tax but no National Insurance, and Preshift

241
00:16:46.806 --> 00:16:51.354
shows the N I saved, the VAT position and the date it must be paid by.

242
00:16:51.805 --> 00:16:56.094
Pay periods runs the close by payroll across a company's sites.

243
00:16:56.094 --> 00:17:01.609
Lock the rota, approve time cards, and pass hours to payroll by the cut off, with

244
00:17:01.609 --> 00:17:04.741
the pay day shown and overdue periods flagged.

245
00:17:05.191 --> 00:17:06.148
Pay approvals.

246
00:17:06.148 --> 00:17:09.566
A change to anyone's rate or salary is a proposal.

247
00:17:09.566 --> 00:17:16.197
Their current pay stays in force until the finance director approves it with their authenticator.

248
00:17:16.197 --> 00:17:22.280
Nobody approves their own proposal or their own pay, and every change shows its full cost

249
00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:22.759
a year.

250
00:17:26.927 --> 00:17:31.575
HR overview puts everything a manager must act on in one list.

251
00:17:31.575 --> 00:17:35.023
Headcount, turnover, absence, and each action:

252
00:17:35.023 --> 00:17:42.069
no return to work conversation, a licence expired, a contract never signed, a fit note missing

253
00:17:42.069 --> 00:17:43.343
after seven days.

254
00:17:43.794 --> 00:17:46.001
Staff holds each employee record:

255
00:17:46.001 --> 00:17:52.823
details, roles, contract and pay, right to work with copies of the documents checked, availability and

256
00:17:52.823 --> 00:17:53.224
leave.

257
00:17:53.224 --> 00:17:59.109
Each record is checked before it reaches the rota, so someone without the right to work,

258
00:17:59.109 --> 00:18:02.586
or paid below the legal minimum, cannot be rostered.

259
00:18:03.036 --> 00:18:06.943
Open a person and their whole file is here, tab by tab:

260
00:18:06.943 --> 00:18:13.620
contract, pay, right to work, training, documents to sign in the staff app, and their history.

261
00:18:14.071 --> 00:18:20.606
Messages keeps one thread per person with their managers, and announcements to a whole site with

262
00:18:20.606 --> 00:18:21.831
who has read them.

263
00:18:21.831 --> 00:18:27.141
Rota notices go out by the app, WhatsApp, text or email, as each person chose.

264
00:18:27.141 --> 00:18:33.607
Everything about work is on record in one place, not scattered across personal WhatsApp groups.

265
00:18:34.058 --> 00:18:40.267
Onboarding gives each new person one checklist, from sixty days before their first day to ninety

266
00:18:40.267 --> 00:18:43.371
days after it, in the order a GM should work it.

267
00:18:43.371 --> 00:18:48.738
The legal steps by day one, payroll and clocking in the first week, training in the

268
00:18:48.738 --> 00:18:49.514
first month.

269
00:18:53.677 --> 00:18:58.947
Wellbeing reads the last four weeks and the fortnight ahead for each person.

270
00:18:58.947 --> 00:19:04.840
Long weeks, runs of days, a close then an open, late finishes, no weekend off, missed

271
00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:06.157
breaks, no holiday.

272
00:19:06.157 --> 00:19:11.635
None of these breaks the law, but each one is a conversation to have this week,

273
00:19:11.635 --> 00:19:13.645
with the next step suggested.

274
00:19:14.096 --> 00:19:20.503
Holiday tracks each person's entitlement for their company's leave year, and the holiday pay provision in

275
00:19:20.503 --> 00:19:20.930
pounds:

276
00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:24.224
earned and not yet taken, ready for the balance sheet.

277
00:19:24.675 --> 00:19:31.583
Absence records sickness and other leave, scores the Bradford factor, and flags every return to work

278
00:19:31.583 --> 00:19:33.379
conversation not yet held.

279
00:19:33.379 --> 00:19:36.003
The cheapest absence control there is.

280
00:19:36.453 --> 00:19:40.541
Training is a matrix of required certificates by role.

281
00:19:40.541 --> 00:19:44.023
Food hygiene, allergens, licensing, first aid.

282
00:19:44.023 --> 00:19:51.139
It shows what an environmental health or licensing visit would find today, and what expires in

283
00:19:51.139 --> 00:19:52.653
the next sixty days.

284
00:19:53.103 --> 00:20:00.017
Probation and reviews tracks probation end dates, so none runs out by default, plus appraisals and

285
00:20:00.017 --> 00:20:02.556
one to ones that are due or overdue.

286
00:20:02.556 --> 00:20:09.399
Cases holds disciplinary and grievance cases, confidential, with the ACAS steps and their timing.

287
00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:15.918
Retention scores who is likely to leave, and why, from what the system already holds:

288
00:20:15.918 --> 00:20:20.344
clocked hours, early finishes, breaks, closes, tenure and pay.

289
00:20:20.344 --> 00:20:25.840
Every point has a reason and a fix, and the replacement cost at risk is shown

290
00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:26.554
in pounds.

291
00:20:27.004 --> 00:20:32.585
Employment rights covers the Employment Rights Act 2025 for zero and low hours workers:

292
00:20:32.585 --> 00:20:38.101
short notice pay owed when a shift is cancelled or cut, and offers of guaranteed hours

293
00:20:38.101 --> 00:20:40.667
that reflect what people regularly work.

294
00:20:40.667 --> 00:20:44.836
The thresholds are settings, ready for when the regulations land.

295
00:20:49.012 --> 00:20:55.477
Labour cost shows every pound payroll will charge, person by person, split into wages, holiday accrual,

296
00:20:55.477 --> 00:21:01.440
employer N I and pension, with rostered hours against contract and a flag wherever the business

297
00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:03.700
is paying for hours it is not using.

298
00:21:04.151 --> 00:21:04.583
Close.

299
00:21:04.583 --> 00:21:10.343
The labour accrual journals, one per company, by role nominal and site tracking.

300
00:21:10.343 --> 00:21:15.383
Post these at week end and the P and L carries true labour on day one.

301
00:21:15.383 --> 00:21:18.695
That is what makes a three day close possible.

302
00:21:19.146 --> 00:21:24.285
Cost lands in the company whose site the work was done at, and the wages accrual

303
00:21:24.285 --> 00:21:28.719
stays with the employer, with the intercompany recharge between them.

304
00:21:28.719 --> 00:21:34.180
Employment Allowance is used against employer N I week by week as payroll applies it.

305
00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:37.842
Download the Xero journal, or post it straight into Xero.

306
00:21:38.293 --> 00:21:38.891
Reports.

307
00:21:38.891 --> 00:21:46.300
GM scorecards ranked on habits before results, the labour trend over four, eight or thirteen weeks,

308
00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:53.485
cost by role and by area, rota against actual, takings, forecast accuracy, and payroll accuracy.

309
00:21:53.936 --> 00:21:58.504
Programme is the twelve week Williams, Stanley labour programme:

310
00:21:58.504 --> 00:22:01.002
Baseline, Control, Optimise, Embed.

311
00:22:01.002 --> 00:22:07.498
Milestones are proved by the site's own data, and the saving is verified against a baseline

312
00:22:07.498 --> 00:22:08.783
from the accounts.

313
00:22:08.783 --> 00:22:13.280
Benchmarks compare your sites with other operators, anonymised.

314
00:22:13.730 --> 00:22:16.175
Prime cost is labour plus cost of sales:

315
00:22:16.175 --> 00:22:21.187
what the two costs a site controls take from every pound sold, with food and drink

316
00:22:21.187 --> 00:22:25.466
margin against what the recipes say, and the leakage in pounds a year.

317
00:22:25.917 --> 00:22:31.052
Compliance risk prices compliance the way a regulator or tribunal would.

318
00:22:31.052 --> 00:22:37.541
Minimum wage arrears owed now, the penalty ceiling, Working Time breaches on clocked hours.

319
00:22:37.541 --> 00:22:40.965
Find the breach first, and the penalties shrink.

320
00:22:41.416 --> 00:22:48.070
Labour cash shows what each company pays out for its people over the next thirteen weeks,

321
00:22:48.070 --> 00:22:48.743
and when.

322
00:22:48.743 --> 00:22:53.678
Net pay on each pay day, tronc, PAYE and N I to HMRC by the twenty

323
00:22:53.678 --> 00:22:55.249
second, and pensions.

324
00:22:55.249 --> 00:23:00.931
A strong month on the rota is a larger HMRC bill about six weeks later, seen

325
00:23:00.931 --> 00:23:02.128
before it lands.

326
00:23:06.289 --> 00:23:12.328
Set up holds the companies that employ your staff, the sites they trade from, the roles

327
00:23:12.328 --> 00:23:14.966
you roster, and how busy each site is.

328
00:23:14.966 --> 00:23:20.728
Labour cost, the forecast build, compliance and the close journal all run off this.

329
00:23:20.728 --> 00:23:26.003
A site can be split into areas, front of house, back of house, a bakery, and

330
00:23:26.003 --> 00:23:28.225
labour is then reported by area.

331
00:23:28.676 --> 00:23:35.337
Access sets roles for operators, Williams Stanley people and outsiders, scoped by site with start and

332
00:23:35.337 --> 00:23:35.997
end dates.

333
00:23:35.997 --> 00:23:42.328
Nobody grants beyond their own access, paired duties such as setting pay and running payroll are

334
00:23:42.328 --> 00:23:45.692
kept apart, and every change is in the audit trail.

335
00:23:46.143 --> 00:23:50.394
Integrations shows every connection and whether it is working:

336
00:23:50.394 --> 00:23:56.291
the till, TeamPay for each PAYE scheme, Xero, card readers, the staff app and the open

337
00:23:56.291 --> 00:23:56.566
API.

338
00:23:56.566 --> 00:24:01.503
Any card not showing connected is a step someone is still doing by hand.

339
00:24:01.953 --> 00:24:07.970
GDPR keeps the request log for access, erasure and the rest, with the one month deadline,

340
00:24:07.970 --> 00:24:15.408
one click subject access export, retention and deletion, and the policy document that holding sickness records

341
00:24:15.408 --> 00:24:16.017
requires.

342
00:24:16.467 --> 00:24:23.228
Settings connects the till, Claude, email and messaging channels, and makes API keys and webhooks for

343
00:24:23.228 --> 00:24:24.165
other systems.

344
00:24:24.165 --> 00:24:29.654
Features lets an owner switch off the parts of Preshift the business does not use.

345
00:24:29.654 --> 00:24:33.939
Nothing is deleted, and switching back on restores it as it was.

346
00:24:34.389 --> 00:24:37.456
Billing holds the trial and subscription.

347
00:24:37.456 --> 00:24:42.244
Your profile keeps your own details, password and authenticator.

348
00:24:42.244 --> 00:24:49.575
Under Help, How to guides for GMs, and Support, answered by your Williams, Stanley client partner.

349
00:24:49.575 --> 00:24:55.410
And API docs opens the full REST API, with an MCP connector so Claude can work

350
00:24:55.410 --> 00:24:56.757
the rota directly.

351
00:24:57.714 --> 00:25:00.984
This is the staff app, on each person's own phone.

352
00:25:00.984 --> 00:25:06.282
Today shows whether they are clocked in, their next shift and their recent hours.

353
00:25:06.282 --> 00:25:12.496
Where the site allows phone clocking, they clock in here, inside the geofence, and record their

354
00:25:12.496 --> 00:25:12.954
breaks.

355
00:25:13.404 --> 00:25:18.847
They can say how their week was, privately, ask for a chat with their manager, and

356
00:25:18.847 --> 00:25:20.772
set a PIN for the kiosk iPad.

357
00:25:21.223 --> 00:25:25.688
The Rota tab shows their own published shifts and who they work with.

358
00:25:25.688 --> 00:25:30.607
They can offer a shift to a named colleague, swap, or pick up an open shift.

359
00:25:31.057 --> 00:25:37.610
Requests is where they ask for holiday against their balance, time off, report sickness, and set

360
00:25:37.610 --> 00:25:38.497
availability.

361
00:25:38.948 --> 00:25:41.933
Pay shows their payslips, and their tips.

362
00:25:41.933 --> 00:25:47.684
Inbox holds every message from their managers, announcements, and rota notices.

363
00:25:48.638 --> 00:25:49.786
That is Preshift.

364
00:25:49.786 --> 00:25:55.458
A rota built from the forecast, costed the way payroll will cost it, legal before it

365
00:25:55.458 --> 00:25:59.172
is published, and in the ledger before payroll has run.

366
00:25:59.172 --> 00:26:03.494
The numbers reach the operator while the decision still matters.
